# Maintainer: flavio <flaviofm99@gmail.com>
#
# 0.20.0: new `phi fan` verb — real PWM fan control via the standard Linux
# hwmon ABI (status/list/set), confirmed live against zotac's nct6798 chip
# (a real hwmon PWM interface, official lm_sensors + in-kernel driver, no
# AUR); the privileged write path needs the companion phios-dotfiles
# sudoers drop-in (49-phi-fan), never applied by this repo. Also:
# `internal/state` gains theme.schedule/theme.schedule-start/theme.
# schedule-end for phi-shell's live auto light/dark theme option, and
# `internal/query`'s image results now open through phi-shell's own native
# floating image window (`qs ipc call image open`) instead of a bare `imv`
# invocation. Tagged v0.20.0 on `main` (fast-forwarded from `dev`, a clean
# 6-commit gap, build+tests verified before tagging).
#
# 0.19.0: `phi agent project` gains a way to leave the active project
# (`--none`), so the agent panel isn't stuck scoped to one project forever.
# Tagged v0.19.0.
#
# 0.18.0: `phi query` gains a stopwatch runner provider (StopwatchProvider),
# recognising "stopwatch", "stopwatch start/resume", "stopwatch pause/stop",
# "stopwatch reset", "stopwatch lap" in the launcher bar, each handed to
# phi-shell as a `qs ipc call stopwatch <verb>`. Companion to the existing
# timer/alarm provider; pairs with phi-shell's new Services/Stopwatch.qml.
# Tagged v0.18.0.
#
# 0.17.0: `phi agent ask`/`phi agent code` surface the real failure instead
# of a raw JSON dump or a bare containment error (a rejected turn's
# provider message; which A2 support systemd unit isn't running) — the AI
# agent subsystem's mechanics were already sound, this fixes every state
# that used to fail silently. Also folds in runner-bar/`phi query` work
# since 0.16.1: the "phi " command prefix routing, a timer/alarm provider,
# full category ranking order (+ ask-ai-agent), opening images via `imv`
# explicitly, hibernate/reboot/shutdown system actions; `phi state`
# nightmode.schedule keys; an `internal/mathx` implicit-plot fix. Tagged
# v0.17.0 — NOTE: tagged directly on `phi`'s `dev` (not `main`, the usual
# convention — AGENTS.md rule 1 leaves merging dev into main to the user,
# so it wasn't done here); the tag itself still resolves and builds fine
# either way, since `source=` below fetches by tag name, not by branch.
#
# 0.16.1: `phi firewall blocked` greps the kernel log for `phi-fw` instead
# of `phi-fw:` — a literal ':' in the pinned sudoers command argument is a
# parse error (`visudo -cf` rejects the file). The exact `phi-fw:` filter
# still runs in-process. Ships alongside 49-phi-firewall's matching fix.
# Tagged v0.16.1.
#
# 0.16.0: `phi firewall` (Out-of-plan: firewall) — an nftables inbound
# firewall behind ~/.config/phi/firewall.json: status / enable / disable /
# preset (home|public|paranoid) / allow / remove / log / blocked. Enforced
# as one `table inet phi`, applied via sudo -n and persisted to
# /etc/nftables.conf. Tagged v0.16.0 at the firewall merge.
#
# 0.15.0: shell-features SF-2 — `phi vpn` now sees /etc/wireguard configs
# and running interfaces (not just its own dir), plus `phi vpn import` /
# `phi vpn forget` for the settings-panel WireGuard management.
# Tagged v0.15.0 at the shell-features merge.
#
# 0.14.0: settings-overhaul phi verbs (OOP-37…OOP-47 — `phi vpn` WireGuard
# control, `phi wallpaper` procedural textures + state keys, `phi theme
# contrast`, `phi pkg` system-state listing) + the advanced runner
# calculator / converter (OOP-48 — `internal/mathx`, `Result.Rich`).
# Tagged v0.14.0 at the converter-calc-magnifier merge.
#
# 0.13.0: agent panel rework (Out-of-plan OOP-26) — three-level memory,
# structured projects, transcript mirror, A2 session store. Tagged v0.13.0.
pkgname=phi
pkgver=0.20.0
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc="phiOS unified CLI"
arch=('x86_64')
url="https://github.com/phiOS-git/phi"
license=('custom')
makedepends=('go' 'git')
source=("git+https://github.com/phiOS-git/phi.git#tag=v${pkgver}")
sha256sums=('SKIP')

build() {
	cd "$srcdir/phi"
	export CGO_ENABLED=0
	# internal/build.Version is "dev" in a local checkout; this is the only
	# place that ever overwrites it (phi/CLAUDE.md, phi/internal/build/build.go).
	go build -trimpath -ldflags "-s -w -X phi/internal/build.Version=${pkgver}" -o phi ./cmd/phi
}

check() {
	cd "$srcdir/phi"
	go vet ./...
}

package() {
	cd "$srcdir/phi"
	install -Dm755 phi "$pkgdir/usr/bin/phi"

	# Completions and the man page are generated here, by the freshly built
	# binary itself, from its own Commands list (internal/view/view.go) —
	# never checked into any repository (S-15 DONE WHEN: "regenerated by
	# the build, not committed by hand"). The .1 file is installed
	# uncompressed; makepkg's own tidy step gzips usr/share/man/* by
	# default, unverified here since no real makepkg run was available off-
	# machine.
	./phi completion zsh > phi.zsh-completion
	install -Dm644 phi.zsh-completion "$pkgdir/usr/share/zsh/site-functions/_phi"

	./phi man > phi.1
	install -Dm644 phi.1 "$pkgdir/usr/share/man/man1/phi.1"
}
